 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-24: biome atmosphere: a unique sky, fog, haze, clouds and stars per biome, eased in real time (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device; +5 tests in `world::atmos`, +1 in `world::sky`; run `cargo test --lib atmos sky` first, then look at it).
+    - `world/atmos.rs` (new, pure): `of(Biome)` = the look of each of the 19 biomes (the table to tune: day colours of the sky top, horizon = fog, haze band, exp² fog density, cloud tint / cover / speed, star tint / brightness, gradient exponent). `Atmos::update` averages the looks of 9 columns (centre + a ring of 48 blocks) four times a second and chases that goal with `TAU` = 2 s in real seconds (`1 - exp(-dt / TAU)`: frame rate independent); `reset` makes the next update jump (new world, Nether). `Atmos::frame(angle, rain, thunder)` gives the renderers a `Frame`. The vanilla colours (`world::sky`) are kept and multiplied by `biome noon colour / vanilla noon colour`, so at noon the sky is exactly the table's colour, night stays dark, rain and thunder still grey it. The temperature term of the old sky colour is gone (the biome decides the hue); `ChunkManager::temperature_at` is deleted.
+    - Fog: `fogp.z` = the biome's density; the chunk / LoD shaders (WGSL + GLSL) leave `(1 - linear) * exp(-(d z)^2)` of a thing d blocks away, so a swamp is thick at 100 blocks and a mountain is clear, and the LoD's linear fog still hides its edge. Rain raises it x2.5.
+    - Dome (`fs_legacy` in `sky.wgsl`, `sky_dome` in `gles/shaders.rs`; same code in both): horizon -> top by the biome's exponent, then a haze band over the horizon (zero at the horizon itself, so the far terrain's fog colour still meets the sky without a seam).
+    - Clouds (new; the Photon `render/clouds.rs` is an orphan and still not compiled): b1.7.3's fancy clouds as a per-pixel march through 12-block cells, 4 blocks thick, at y 108 (`WorldProvider.getCloudHeight`), drifting along +x at 0.03 blocks a tick x the biome's speed (the drift is integrated on the CPU, so a faster biome changes the speed, never the place). A cell is filled when two octaves of value noise pass the biome's cover threshold (rain adds cover); the ray walks at most 8 cells, hits an underside (0.62) or a side wall (0.86 / 0.76) and the colour melts into the horizon colour by the biome's fog density and with distance. No geometry, no texture, no new pipeline; only pixels the scene left at depth 1 run it.
+    - Stars: the star quads take the biome's tint and brightness (`stars` uniform).
+    - `world::sky::cloud_color` (`World.func_628_d`): white by day, 0.1 / 0.1 / 0.15 at night, greyed by rain (0.6) and thunder (0.2). UNVERIFIED: written from memory, the Java is not in the zip.
+    - UNVERIFIED on a device: the colours in the table (taken by eye from four reference screenshots: teal swamp, lavender, autumn, desert), the cost of the cloud march on low-end GPUs (first levers: 8 -> 5 cells, one noise octave), that the stars drawn after the dome show through dark night clouds, that no clouds are drawn while the eye is above y 112 (a peak), and `u32(i32)` wrap-around in the shaders.
+    - Not done: cloud shadows on the terrain, clouds under the eye above the layer, per-biome cloud height, fog / sky changes inside caves, the LoD's own haze (it only has the shared fog).
 - 2026-10-22 (3): the debug screen shows the render settings, and Dynamic Resolution has a button (type-checked with `cargo check -p mc-rs --lib --tests --target aarch64-linux-android`, 0 errors; not run, not seen on a device; +0 tests, `options::tests::options_screens_flow` taps the new button).
     - Button: `Dynamic Res: ON/OFF` (`Opt::DynamicRes`) is the 12th cell of Video Settings, the free one next to `Renderer`; it flips `Settings::dynamic_res` (`dynamicRes:` in options.txt, on by default). It takes effect at once, no restart: while it is off `lib.rs` pins the scene at `START_PCT` (67%) again and restarts `Drs` from there, so a scale the controller had lowered does not stay stuck; switching it on lets `Drs` move from 67% as at start-up.
     - Debug screen, right panel: `Screen` is the surface only now; new rows `Scene` (size and percent, `gpu::context::scale_pct`), `Dyn. res`, `MSAA` (the sample count in use, `present::scene_samples`, then the setting in brackets: `4x  [auto]`, `4x  [2x (restart)]` when the button was changed since the start), `Post` (`full` / `fast`, `present::fast_post`), `Graphics` (+ smooth lighting) and `Perf` (the frame cap). The bracketed values and the `Dyn. res`, `Graphics` and `Perf` rows are `Settings::text` with the name cut off, so a button and its row cannot disagree. The GLES `Renderer::new` now also stores its samples and final-pass choice in `present` (they were only stored by the wgpu `Gpu::try_init`), or the rows would read `off` / `full` there.
